  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...An upper ridge and Bermuda high pressure will be\ncentered off the coast through Saturday, then becomes suppressed\nlate in the weekend as shortwave energy pushes across the mid- \nAtlantic with more of a zonal pattern developing next week with \na series of shortwave troughs pushing across the area. Precip \nchances will be near climo each day with widely scattered \nshowers and thunderstorms developing each afternoon, then\ndissipating with loss of heating during the evening. The severe\nthreat appears minimal through the period with limited shear \nand forcing. \n\nA gradual warming trend will continue through the period as well\nwith highs in the lower 90s inland through the weekend, then\nwarming in to the mid 90s next week. Temps generally in the mid\nto upper 80s along the coast. The probabilities for Major Heat\nRisk increase to around 60-80% Monday through Thursday of next\nweek.",
